{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThree defensive `except`/`isinstance` arms that decide whether an LLM-tier failure ABORTS or\nDEGRADES have **no test that reaches them** (found by the Step-7 parity sweep in bug\n`wolflike-chevroned-haddock`, `43d4-b8f5-4bb2-417b`). Mutation-proven: reverting each arm to\nits pre-43d4 form (dropping `LLMInputRejectedError`) leaves the entire unit suite green.\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`: the mid-run\n  `except (LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)` arms around `_ex.run_workflow` in\n  `produce_plan_review_verdict` (~:189) and `_run_code_review_gate` (~:522).\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/container_stage.py` warm-call abort in `_run_container` (~:209).\n  `container_stage` has zero referencing tests — its abort-vs-degrade ruling is unpinned.\n\n## Context — reachability (resolves the original \"dead code?\" question)\n\nThe original probe raised in the **agent-step** path, which `interpreter._run_leaf` absorbs\ninto a failed `StepResult` — never escaping `run_workflow`. The **batch-step** path is the raw\nseam: `interpreter._run_batch` calls `runner.run(req, rc.runner)` with **no try**, so batch\nrunner raises propagate raw. Plan-review's `ProductionBatchRunner` -> `run_pass1` **re-raises**\n`LLMUnavailableError` from the chunk pool, and the container warm abort raises **both** types\nup through it — so the plan-review arm is reachable in production (NOT dead code), fed by the\ncontainer arm. Code-review's `CodeReviewBatchRunner._run_criterion` translates\n`LLMUnavailableError` into `SystemicDiscoveryError`, which `discovery.execute_stage` absorbs\n(`systemic_abort=True`, no re-raise) — no in-tree raw raiser found, so that arm is a\n**defensive contract at the run_workflow seam**. Per the coverage-only mandate it is pinned,\nnot removed; the finding is recorded as a ticket comment.\n\n## Approach — coverage only, zero production-code change\n\n1. `tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_midrun_fail_closed.py`\n   - Plan-review arm: monkeypatch `executor.run_workflow` to raise (a) `LLMUnavailableError`,\n     (b) `LLMInputRejectedError` (the established `test_gate_engine_cutover.py` seam, incl.\n     the `_gate_doc` skeleton); drive `produce_plan_review_verdict` with `FakeRunner`; assert\n     the degraded INDETERMINATE verdict (never PASS, `llm_ran is False`) AND the\n     `emit_gate_error` sidecar call (kwargs-tolerant recorder — the arm threads `diagnostic=`).\n   - Code-review arm: same injection through `produce_code_review_verdict` (`enabled=True`,\n     `target_ticket` set so the sidecar fires, WS4's `_local_gate_source` autouse fixture\n     copied to avoid the CI shallow-checkout hang); assert INDETERMINATE + sidecar for both\n     types.\n   - Seam-fidelity: a REAL `run_workflow` over a minimal valid batch-step doc (the\n     `test_batch_step.py` `_wf` shape) with an injected batch runner that raises — assert both\n     types propagate RAW (`pytest.raises`), pinning `_run_batch`'s no-try contract that makes\n     the mid-run arms reachable.\n\n2. `tests/unit/test_container_warm_abort.py` (sibling of `test_container_roster.py`)\n   - Drive the REAL `_run_container` with `passes.pass1_container` monkeypatched at the\n     model-call boundary. Fixture: `PlanContext(largest_window_tokens=50_000)` (budget 13_000\n     tokens), plan text ~20_000 chars (~5_000 tokens >= the 4_096 cache floor), two children\n     ~28_000 chars each (~7_000 tokens) -> `pack_container_bins` yields two single-child bins\n     -> the warm gate is MET; the warm call is the first `pass1_container` invocation.\n   - `LLMUnavailableError` on warm -> `pytest.raises` + exactly ONE call (abort, no fan-out).\n   - `LLMInputRejectedError` on warm -> same abort assertions (the 43d4 arm).\n   - Negative control: `ValueError` on warm -> no raise; degrades to direct fan-out of ALL\n     pairings (3 calls: failed warm + 2 pool re-runs), `coverage[\"container\"][\"warmed\"]` False.\n\n## Scope\n\n- IN: the two new test files; ticket comments recording the reachability analysis and the\n  mutation-check transcript.\n- OUT (non-goals): any change to `gate_dispatch.py`, `container_stage.py`, `pass1.py`,\n  `interpreter.py` or any production module; removing the code-review arm; new lint/CI\n  machinery. If a test exposes a genuine behavioral divergence, a new bug ticket is filed and\n  linked `discovered_from` this one instead of changing gate behavior here.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN mutation protocol)\n\nRED — each new test must FIRE against the gap it covers, then the mutation is reverted:\n- Mutant A: revert both gate_dispatch arms to `except LLMUnavailableError` only -> the two\n  input-rejected mid-run tests FAIL (the exception escapes).\n- Mutant B: narrow the container isinstance to `LLMUnavailableError` only -> the\n  input-rejected abort test FAILS (degrades instead of raising).\n- Mutant C: remove the container abort arm entirely -> both abort tests FAIL.\nOutputs recorded in a ticket comment; tree restored (`git diff --stat` clean on `src/`).\n\nGREEN — on unmutated code: both new files pass, plus `tests/unit/test_gate_engine_cutover.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_code_review_ws4.py`, `tests/unit/workflow/test_batch_step.py`,\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_warmup.py`. Gates: `make lint`, `make typecheck`,\n`python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` (new=0 increased=0). No production file\nchanges -> module-size cap unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Tests reach the mid-run plan-review arm for BOTH `LLMUnavailableError` and\n      `LLMInputRejectedError`, asserting the degraded INDETERMINATE verdict plus the emitted\n      `gate_error_v1` sidecar (`pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_midrun_fail_closed.py -q`).\n- [ ] The same for the mid-run code-review arm; its reachability status (defensive seam\n      contract — systemic errors are translated and absorbed upstream; no in-tree raw raiser)\n      is recorded as a ticket comment, resolving the remove-or-test question as test-as-contract.\n- [ ] A seam-fidelity test proves batch-runner `LLMUnavailableError`/`LLMInputRejectedError`\n      propagate RAW out of a real `run_workflow` (pinning `_run_batch`'s no-try contract).\n- [ ] Tests drive `_run_container`'s REAL warm-call path: both systemic types abort the\n      fan-out (raise, exactly one model call); a non-systemic failure degrades to direct\n      fan-out (negative control).\n- [ ] Each new test is shown to FAIL under its arm's mutation (Mutants A/B/C), transcript\n      recorded in a ticket comment, mutations reverted.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the complexity ratchet pass; no `src/rebar` file is\n      modified by this change."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787381673320773001,"uuid":"14586f2a-ffd6-476c-baed-c07d23dd1181"}